================================================================================
Have I Been Pwned — Pwned Passwords
================================================================================

The embedded breached-password corpus
(services/api/internal/breachlist/breached-passwords.bin), used by the
password breach-corpus screen (NIST SP 800-63B §5.1.1.2), is derived from the
breach-frequency data published by Have I Been Pwned (Pwned Passwords),
created and maintained by Troy Hunt.

    Source:  Have I Been Pwned — Pwned Passwords
             https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords
    Author:  Troy Hunt
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Only the data (the set of compromised-password SHA-1 digests) is embedded; the
SHA-1 digest functions purely as a lookup index, not as a password-storage
primitive (AxiaOps stores passwords with argon2id). The
HaveIBeenPwned/PwnedPasswordsDownloader tool is used only to *generate* the
asset and is NOT embedded, so its separate licence does not propagate into the
AxiaOps binaries.

The currently shipped asset is a curated bootstrap seed of the most-prevalent
breached passwords (public knowledge), not the full HIBP top-1M corpus. See
docs/breachlist-provenance.md for the manifest (source, N, SHA-256) and the
procedure to swap in the full HIBP corpus.
